      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "REA John Lee are delighted to present to the market this attractive rural property comprising a derelict cottage dwelling together with a range of traditional outbuildings, standing on a generous site extending to approximately 0.416 hectares / 1.03 acres. Situated in a pleasant countryside setting, the property offers an excellent opportunity for a purchaser seeking a renovation or redevelopment project. The existing cottage requires complete refurbishment, while the adjoining outbuildings provide useful storage and offer additional potential, subject to any necessary planning permission. The site is of a manageable size and enjoys ample space surrounding the dwelling, providing scope for landscaped gardens, parking and further enhancement. Its traditional character and rural setting make it particularly suitable for those wishing to create a distinctive country residence. The property is conveniently located within easy reach of Cappamore village and the surrounding towns and villages of Murroe, Newport and Castleconnell, while Limerick City is also within comfortable commuting distance.\nThis is a rare opportunity to acquire a traditional cottage property with substantial potential in an established rural location.This property could potentially be eligible for grants up to ?70,000 with the Cro Cnaithe Fund, which is available for properties intended for rental as well as owner-occupied homes undergoing refurbishment. This grant may also be combined with the Sustainable Energy Authority of Ireland`s Better Energy Home Scheme, which could potentially offer a further ?26,750 in support. Full Details from the agent."
